[181.835677, "i", "cat > BUGFIX_SUMMARY.md << 'EOF'\n# Distributed TF-IDF Pipeline Bug Fix Summary\n\n## Problem\nThe distributed feature extraction pipeline was producing incorrect output:\n- Only 12k rows instead of 50k (missing data)\n- Invalid tf-idf scores > 1.0 (mathematically impossible)\n- No errors or crashes (silent data corruption)\n\n## Root Causes Identified\n\n### 1. **Incorrect Vocabulary Management (CRITICAL)**\nEach worker was calling `vectorizer.fit_transform()` on individual chunks:\n```python\n# WRONG - each chunk gets its own vocabulary\nvectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(max_features=100)\ntfidf_matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(texts)  # Fits on chunk only!\n```\n\n**Why this caused invalid scores:**\n- TF-IDF requires a unified vocabulary across ALL documents\n- Each chunk built its own vocabulary with different terms\n- IDF (inverse document frequency) was calculated only within each chunk\n- This produced invalid scores and incompatible feature columns\n\n### 2. **Column Misalignment**\nWorkers returned DataFrames with different colu"]
[181.835846, "i", "mn names (different vocabularies):\n- Worker 1 chunk: columns ['apple', 'banana', 'cherry', ...]\n- Worker 2 chunk: columns ['dog', 'elephant', 'fox', ...]\n- Coordinator's `pd.concat()` created union of all columns, filling missing values\n- Result: sparse, misaligned data with wrong dimensions\n\n### 3. **Message Loss at Startup**\nCoordinator sent chunks immediately after binding sockets:\n```python\nsender.bind(\"tcp://127.0.0.1:5557\")\n# Immediately sends chunks - workers not connected yet!\nfor chunk in chunks:\n    sender.send(chunk)\n```\nZeroMQ PUSH sockets can drop messages if no PULL sockets are connected.\n\n### 4. **Poor Result Tracking**\nCoordinator used a list instead of dict for results:\n```python\nresults = []  # Can't detect missing chunks\nresults.append(result_df)  # No chunk ID tracking\n```\nTimeout-based completion meant lost chunks went undetected.\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### Fix 1: Unified Vocabulary (coordinator.py)\n```python\n# Fit vectorizer on ALL data ONCE\nvectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(max_features=100)\ntex"]
[181.835909, "i", "ts = df[\"text\"].tolist()\nvectorizer.fit(texts)  # Build vocabulary from all 50k documents\n\n# Send fitted vectorizer to all workers\nfor i in range(3):\n    sender.send(pickle.dumps((\"VECTORIZER\", vectorizer)))\n```\n\n### Fix 2: Transform-Only in Workers (worker.py)\n```python\n# Receive fitted vectorizer from coordinator\nmsg_type, vectorizer = pickle.loads(receiver.recv())\n\n# Use transform() only - don't fit!\ntfidf_matrix = vectorizer.transform(texts)  # Uses shared vocabulary\n```\n\n### Fix 3: Startup Synchronization (coordinator.py)\n```python\n# Wait for workers to connect\ntime.sleep(2)\n\n# Send vectorizer first\nfor i in range(3):\n    sender.send(vectorizer_msg)\ntime.sleep(0.5)\n\n# Then send chunks\nfor chunk_id, chunk in enumerate(chunks):\n    sender.send(chunk_msg)\n```\n\n### Fix 4: Proper Result Tracking (coordinator.py)\n```python\n# Use dict to track results by chunk_id\nresults = {}\nwhile len(results) < num_chunks:\n    chunk_id, result_df = pickle.loads(receiver.recv())\n    results[chunk_id] = result_df\n\n# Check for m"]
[181.83592, "o", "cat > BUGFIX_SUMMARY.md << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[181.835969, "i", "issing chunks\nif len(results) < num_chunks:\n    missing = set(range(num_chunks)) - set(results.keys())\n    print(f\"Missing chunks: {missing}\")\n\n# Aggregate in correct order\nordered_results = [results[i] for i in sorted(results.keys())]\nfinal_df = pd.concat(ordered_results, ignore_index=True)\n```\n\n### Fix 5: Proper Termination (both files)\n```python\n# Coordinator sends DONE signals\nfor i in range(3):\n    sender.send(pickle.dumps((\"DONE\", None, None)))\n\n# Workers handle DONE signal\nif msg_type == \"DONE\":\n    break\n```\n\n## Results\n\n**Before fixes:**\n- Output: 12,000 rows\n- Value range: [0.0, >1.0] ❌\n- Comparison to reference: Failed\n\n**After fixes:**\n- Output: 50,000 rows ✓\n- Value range: [0.0, 0.7998] ✓\n- Comparison to reference: **PERFECT MATCH (0.0 difference)** ✓\n\n## Key Lesson\n\nFor distributed TF-IDF (or any ML feature extraction):\n1. **Fit once on all data** to build vocabulary/statistics\n2. **Share the fitted model** with all workers\n3. **Workers only transform** using the shared model\n4. Never fi"]
[181.835996, "o", "ts = df[\"text\"].tolist()\r\nvectorizer.fit(texts)  # Build vocabulary from all 50k documents\r\n\r\n# Send fitted vectorizer to all workers\r\nfor i in range(3):\r\n    sender.send(pickle.dumps((\"VECTORIZER\", vectorizer)))\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Fix 2: "]
[181.836046, "i", "t on subsets - it breaks the mathematical assumptions!\nEOF\n"]
